KFAC  = (PI*(H/2))/(4*B*B) * SQRT(GG2/(6*RHO*(1-NU_iso)))
*DIM, FRA2, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, MIDX, ARRAY, NMODES
*DIM, LFEA, ARRAY, NMODES
*DO, I, 1, NMODES
  *GET, FRA2(I), MODE, I, FREQ
  MIDX(I) = I
  LFEA(I) = FRA2(I)/KFAC
*ENDDO
! FIXED 2026-09-06: single whole-array *VWRITE call -- NEVER *VWRITE
! inside a *DO loop. The old per-iteration-scalar *VWRITE call this
! replaced silently garbled its own output (confirmed: this exact
! block's Lambda_FE column was all-zero on disk with non-monotonic
! mode numbering before this fix). See project memory
! ansys-kfac-runtime-bug.md and paper2-literature-review-gap-2026-09-05.md.
*CFOPEN, rect_ff_asym_mesh2_lob300, txt
*VWRITE
('mode      f[Hz]           Lambda_FE    (ASYM=ODD parity; SHELL281 x90/y30; must agree with x60/y20 <0.3%)')
*VWRITE, MIDX(1), FRA2(1), LFEA(1)
(F4.0, 3X, E14.6, 3X, F12.6)
*CFCLOS
FINISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  AFTER RUNNING (order matters):
!   0. Convergence gate per pass (<0.3%, mesh1 vs mesh2).
!   1. Do NOT use the deck Lambda_FE column (runtime SQRT missing).
!      Convert the first mode-1 *VWRITE Hz block with KFAC=24.6644:
!      Lambda = f[Hz] / 24.6644. Discard near-zero (rigid-body) Hz and
!      anything implying f>30 Hz.
!   2. Compare SYMM-pass Lambdas to l/b=3.0 SYM B-pass candidates
!      (0.240, 1.320, 1.920, 2.160, 2.260); ASYM-pass to ANTI candidates (0.540, 0.940, 1.160, 1.520, 1.640, 1.920, 2.120, 2.260).
!      Cross-parity matches do not count. Candidates are job 2453876
!      PAPER_CANDIDATES (Screen B persist, n_cpair=3, |dL|<=0.01) -- NOT
!      yet FE-validated. Exclude the known SYM 0.41 leak (and at l/b=3.0
!      the ANTI 0.440 member of the 0.46 leak family).
!      Do NOT treat ANTI 0.440 as a paper candidate (0.46-family leak
!      that Screen B passed only because 0.440 is just outside +/-0.015
!      of 0.460). SYM 0.41 is the known leak. ANTI 1.640 is the recurring extra.
!   3. If every candidate misses by a common factor, suspect KFAC / Hz
!      extraction before the physics.
! ===========================================================================
